<p>South Africa has appointed veteran politician Roelf Meyer as its next ambassador to the United States, turning to a senior Afrikaner figure best known for helping negotiate the end of apartheid as Pretoria tries to steady a strained relationship with Washington. President Cyril Ramaphosa’s office confirmed the appointment, filling a Washington post that had stood vacant since former ambassador Ebrahim Rasool was expelled in 2025. Meyer, 78, sat across from Ramaphosa in the 1993-94 negotiations that led South Africa into democracy. His selection is widely seen as an effort to reopen dialogue after more than a year of unusually tense diplomacy between Pretoria and Washington.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Kb5Sopk5GhPjmns6LbduSu3YCQ_GwSq1haA8cWatnu1s7TH6UXhf8QELPirkco5BZyFfZiqsH6LCxliXYmPHMQAsXO136FU6ogRQbf6pm4uu-pMjnKc0nNxnnjwqxtY2txzXWNVfj8Zq_SSsThfABEXV2kwetPezwCcebCD1_b6466bp5U6KEQZil13HebwJL1I8TMrQ8Uyv7g400c1sPPl3Gpj-ea6w5uyNSjmTGJ5qchDfigUSrGmWwUY9pg3igEFSGg4vV5X3n6ystnYS0xMV' alt='Roelf Meyer, who played a key role in negotiations to end white-minority rule in South Africa, has been named ambassador to the United States.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Long-vacant post: South Africa went more than a year without an ambassador in Washington after Rasool was declared persona non grata in March 2025 over webinar remarks criticizing the Trump administration and the MAGA movement.</li><li>Career arc: Before he became known as a bridge-builder, Meyer entered parliament in 1979 and served in senior National Party governments under Pieter Botha and FW de Klerk, including as defense minister and constitutional affairs minister.</li><li>Heavy agenda: Meyer arrives amid broader disputes over South Africa’s Black empowerment policies, its BRICS alignment, its genocide case against Israel, US allegations that Pretoria has grown too close to Iran, and false claims about a &quot;white genocide&quot; in the country.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>South African presidency: Ramaphosa’s office presented Meyer as a key architect of constitutional democracy and, according to RT, &quot;a true citizen committed to a non-racial South Africa,&quot; stressing his nation-building credentials rather than his National Party past. (<a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202604150109.html'>allAfrica</a>, <a href='https://www.rt.com/africa/638443-south-africa-appoints-former-apartheid-era-minister-us-envoy/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Trump administration: Washington’s earlier handling of Rasool’s case showed a sharply confrontational stance, with Secretary of State Marco Rubio saying the envoy was &quot;no longer welcome&quot; after comments about the MAGA movement, according to RT’s account. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/africa/638443-south-africa-appoints-former-apartheid-era-minister-us-envoy/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Several outlets highlighted the symbolism of sending a prominent Afrikaner to Washington while the Trump administration has amplified attention on white South Africans, suggesting Pretoria is also trying to shift the political optics of the relationship. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-appoints-veteran-afrikaner-politician-roelf-meyer-as-us-ambassador-amid-tense-trump-ties/a-76794872'>DW</a>, <a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/15/south-africa-names-ambassador-us-roelf-meyer'>The Guardian</a>, <a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/15/2026/south-africa-turns-to-afrikaner-as-ambassador-to-us'>Semafor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-appoints-veteran-afrikaner-politician-roelf-meyer-as-us-ambassador-amid-tense-trump-ties/a-76794872'>South Africa appoints veteran Afrikaner politician Roelf Meyer as US ambassador amid tense Trump ties</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/15/2026/south-africa-turns-to-afrikaner-as-ambassador-to-us'>South Africa turns to Afrikaner as ambassador to US</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://w